# Architecture (overview v3.1)

The website **sells and previews**. Full functionality (rating, snapshot) **always requires the app**.

## This repo — landing + web preview

- Marketing landing (existing Next.js base): conversion, SEO, EN/AR, brand. Demos are illustrative.
- Scan/link with **no app**: business card **only**. No rate. No snapshot. Download-app CTA.
- Do not turn public web preview into a second full product.

## Applications

- **Mobile (React Native, iOS + Android):** scan/NFC, full card, rating flow, snapshot, My List, Settings, push as needed.
- **Web app (MERN):** auth, verification, profile, privacy, themes, subscription; still not a substitute for the “no app” preview rule on public QR pages.
- **Backend:** REST, verification, rating engine, reputation, disputes, billing hooks. Cloud/OTP/email/push/stores are client-paid; interface first.

Share one domain model across clients. Score math lives on the server.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — public web preview lets visitors rate or open snapshot
<PublicPreview onRate={submit} showSnapshot />

// ✅ GOOD — no app: card + download; app: rate + snapshot
```
